Complexity Analysis

Let n be the length of the input string.

Time Complexity: O(n) – The algorithm scans the string once, processing each character at most once.
Space Complexity: O(1) – Only a constant number of variables are used.
Key Takeaway

The String to Integer (atoi) problem demonstrates how to implement manual string parsing while handling signs, whitespace, invalid characters, and integer overflow.

The important concepts are:

Character-by-character parsing.
Handling positive and negative signs.
Stopping at the first non-digit character.
Clamping values within the 32-bit signed integer range.

This approach solves the problem in linear time with constant auxiliary space.
